1
00:00:12,336 --> 00:00:20,564
L'auteur soutient que la ville devrait fermer le centre aux voitures. Il estime que c'est la seule solution.
The author argues that the city should close the centre to cars. He believes it's the only solution.

2
00:00:20,664 --> 00:00:27,260
Il met en avant plusieurs arguments : la pollution, le bruit et la sécurité des piétons.
He puts forward several arguments: pollution, noise and pedestrian safety.

3
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:34,244
Il affirme que les commerces n'en souffriraient pas. Mais il ne cite aucune étude.
He claims shops wouldn't suffer. But he cites no study.

4
00:00:34,344 --> 00:00:41,636
Il souligne aussi que la mairie aurait déjà reçu plusieurs plaintes. Mais c'est à vérifier.
He also stresses that the town hall has reportedly already received several complaints. But that needs checking.

5
00:00:41,736 --> 00:00:46,772
Ce conditionnel indique que l'information n'est pas confirmée.
That conditional shows that the information isn't confirmed.

6
00:00:46,872 --> 00:00:54,068
Oui. En résumé, sa position est claire, mais ses preuves sont fragiles.
Yes. In summary, his position is clear, but his evidence is weak.
